Cell[TextData[{
 "There are implemented two methods for generating matrix representations of \
Clifford algebras:\[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]TensorProduct\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote]\
  and \[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]IdealBasis\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote]. The method \
\[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]IdealBasis\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] computes primitive \
idempotent,  left ideal and double sided ideal for matrix  and then generate \
spinor matrix representation. The method is demonstrated and explained in \
Spinor notebook. The other method \[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]TensorProduct\
\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote], uses iterative procedure and generates higher \
algebras representations using matrix representations of lower dimensional \
matrices. All representations are generated from representations of the \
elementary algebras ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubscriptBox["Cl", 
    RowBox[{"p", ",", "q"}]], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "c3530950-c974-4c3c-91ca-dace0d773b69"],
 ", p+q\[LessEqual]2. In fact after we programmed this method we found its \
theoretical confirmation in the article of Marchuk (in translation from \
Russian)."
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.673770213170585*^9, 3.673770271212688*^9}, {
   3.673770498050648*^9, 3.673770512428942*^9}, {3.67377085466058*^9, 
