Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[TextData[{
 "Matrix representations of Clifford algebras ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubscriptBox["Cl", 
    RowBox[{"p", ",", "q"}]], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "8df8d664-bc8b-4a0a-bfbb-6cffff69a9d7"],
 ", p+q>2 && p,q\[LessEqual]7"
}], "Subsection",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.673769332785334*^9, 3.673769392504071*^9}, {
  3.67376947173848*^9, 3.673769497846831*^9}, {3.673769548025817*^9, 
  3.673769569312313*^9}, {3.673857865702308*^9, 3.673857886324916*^9}, {
  3.673932358127437*^9, 3.673932420912707*^9}, {3.682139156265242*^9, 
  3.6821392814452*^9}, {3.682139371717413*^9, 3.682139405020443*^9}, {
  3.68213978051513*^9, 3.682139788189103*^9}, {3.683517797768481*^9, 
  3.683517798150929*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"3a49bfc5-36c0-4bc2-8cd3-\
d2f8cb60eb86"],

Cell["\<\
Below we construct matrix representations for real Clifford algebras, which \
is known to be of dimensions:
\[DoubleStruckCapitalR](2^(n/2)),    if q-p=0,6 (mod 8); 
\[DoubleStruckCapitalC](2^((n-1)/2)),    if q-p=1,5(mod 8); 
\[DoubleStruckCapitalH](2^((n-2)/2)),    if q-p=2,4(mod 8); 
\[DoubleStruckCapitalH](2^((n-3)/2))\[CirclePlus]\[DoubleStruckCapitalH](2^((\
n-3)/2)),   if q-p=3(mod 8); 
\[DoubleStruckCapitalR](2^((n-1)/2))\[CirclePlus]\[DoubleStruckCapitalR](2^((\
n-1)/2)),   if q-p=7(mod 8); \
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.673770213170585*^9, 3.673770271212688*^9}, {
   3.673770498050648*^9, 3.673770512428942*^9}, {3.67377085466058*^9, 
   3.673770874134313*^9}, {3.673847424440953*^9, 3.673847454297884*^9}, {
   3.67384748908961*^9, 3.673847491281632*^9}, {3.67385142912274*^9, 
   3.673851598056488*^9}, {3.673853198231991*^9, 3.673853276480684*^9}, {
   3.673853330115768*^9, 3.673853357100738*^9}, {3.673853613532576*^9, 
   3.673853650616628*^9}, {3.673932571048672*^9, 3.673932870007566*^9}, {
   3.673933020665118*^9, 3.673933121360579*^9}, {3.673954643605199*^9, 
   3.673954896081281*^9}, {3.673955211748288*^9, 3.673955219561568*^9}, {
   3.675673310845051*^9, 3.67567331629103*^9}, {3.675673358390805*^9, 
   3.675673359137947*^9}, {3.67567352896534*^9, 3.675673535300923*^9}, {
   3.67853204996788*^9, 3.678532186339469*^9}, {3.682134982660615*^9, 
   3.682135043365541*^9}, {3.682139802950836*^9, 3.682139831322959*^9}, {
   3.682140091652602*^9, 3.682140444417654*^9}, 3.7788222986697407`*^9, {
   3.822050111852504*^9, 
   3.822050112824129*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"70ef5151-434e-413b-8c0b-\
2b637911ecd8"],

Cell["\<\
For quaternionic representations we also can calculate representation \
matrices of elements from \[DoubleStruckCapitalR] and \
\[DoubleStruckCapitalC]. We also test interesting property of determinant, \
which can serve as definition of matrix representation of Clifford algebra as \
well. All calculations are sorted first by algebras positive, then negative \
signature. \
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->CompressedData["
